1
00:00:00,190 --> 00:00:02,470
Greetings, fellow aliens!

2
00:00:02,470 --> 00:00:05,320
Welcome to the twelveth episode of Earthlings
101.

3
00:00:05,320 --> 00:00:42,089
Today we will learn about the earthlings'
most important sense: Vision, or eyesight.

4
00:00:42,089 --> 00:00:46,059
Vision is the capacity to perceive light in
order to create a mental image of the environment.

5
00:00:46,059 --> 00:00:48,199
But what is light?

6
00:00:48,199 --> 00:00:51,300
Light is electromagnetic radiation wthin a
certain range.

7
00:00:51,300 --> 00:00:56,460
The earth athmosphere filters most radiation
from the sun, except for three ranges of wavelengths:

8
00:00:56,460 --> 00:01:00,260
The radio window, the infrared window, and
the optical window.

9
00:01:00,260 --> 00:01:05,300
The latter is between 300 and 1100 nanometers
- that's the frequency of light.

10
00:01:05,300 --> 00:01:09,970
Earthlings can perceive light between 390
and 700 nanometers - that's called visible

11
00:01:09,970 --> 00:01:10,970
light.

12
00:01:10,970 --> 00:01:15,320
The earthlings perceive light with their eyes
- a pair of globular organs in the head.

13
00:01:15,320 --> 00:01:20,000
Eyes are primitive biocameras: Light falls
through a lense, is focused onto a photosensitive

14
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:24,490
layer called retina, is transformed into electrical
signals, and then...

15
00:01:24,490 --> 00:01:27,420
Well, that's when things become interesting.

16
00:01:27,420 --> 00:01:30,910
Earthling sensor are often compared with the
sensor system of levy drones.

17
00:01:30,910 --> 00:01:35,360
When the Galactic Tax Authority executes a
planetary tax examination, it sends in a Tax

18
00:01:35,360 --> 00:01:39,520
Star which releases millions of levy drones
to the planet's surface.

19
00:01:39,520 --> 00:01:44,250
Each levy drone is equipped with a multitude
of tax assessment sensors, including a sophisticated

20
00:01:44,250 --> 00:01:46,300
high-definition camera.

21
00:01:46,300 --> 00:01:50,520
On first glance, a drone camera seems to work
exactly like an earthling eye:

22
00:01:50,520 --> 00:01:54,800
Light falls through a lense system onto an
array of spectroscopic photoreceptors.

23
00:01:54,800 --> 00:01:58,900
The spectroscopic pixel matrix is then sent
to the central computer where it is processed

24
00:01:58,900 --> 00:02:01,760
and transformed into a 3d voxel model.

25
00:02:01,760 --> 00:02:06,570
Finally, the tax routines compute the monetary
value of each taxable entity.

26
00:02:06,570 --> 00:02:10,860
If you take this - minus the tax part - you
get a very good explanation of how earthling

27
00:02:10,860 --> 00:02:12,450
vision does not work.

28
00:02:12,450 --> 00:02:16,750
Because, from the moment on when the light
hits the retina, earthling vision is completely

29
00:02:16,750 --> 00:02:17,750
different.

30
00:02:17,750 --> 00:02:22,180
In particular, what the eyes send to the brain
is not only pixel data, but also data about

31
00:02:22,180 --> 00:02:24,560
contrast, color contrast and motion.

32
00:02:24,560 --> 00:02:28,860
In other words, the first step of data processing
happens literally within the eyes.

33
00:02:28,860 --> 00:02:33,800
See, the retina consists of light-sensitive
cells, rods and cones.

34
00:02:33,800 --> 00:02:37,640
Above those cells we have a thin layer of
intermediate neurons, which wire them to the

35
00:02:37,640 --> 00:02:39,920
neuro-cables leading to the brain.

36
00:02:39,920 --> 00:02:44,250
Some neurons simply forward information from
the rods and cones, but others provide a clever

37
00:02:44,250 --> 00:02:47,340
lateral wiring to detect contrast or motion.

38
00:02:47,340 --> 00:02:51,140
For example, one neuron might emit a signal
when a certain spot is brighter than it's

39
00:02:51,140 --> 00:02:52,190
neighbourhood.

40
00:02:52,190 --> 00:02:57,580
In consequence, the cell detects contrast,
or, in other words, contours.

41
00:02:57,580 --> 00:03:01,550
Another neuron might only fire when it detects
motion in a certain direction.

42
00:03:01,550 --> 00:03:05,560
Still another neuron emits a signal when it
perceives a color difference between neighbour

43
00:03:05,560 --> 00:03:07,490
spots, and so on.

44
00:03:07,490 --> 00:03:12,930
So, what is sent to the brain is information
about motion, contrast and color contrast.

45
00:03:12,930 --> 00:03:14,849
But where is the information sent?

46
00:03:14,849 --> 00:03:17,800
The eyes are wired to the Thalamus, in the
center of the brain.

47
00:03:17,800 --> 00:03:22,710
"Thalamus" is an ancient word for "inner chamber",
and it's kind of a data connection center.

48
00:03:22,710 --> 00:03:26,160
Whoever sends information to the brain must
pass through the thalamus.

49
00:03:26,160 --> 00:03:29,580
In particular, the eyes are wired to the two
lateral geniculate nuclei -

50
00:03:29,580 --> 00:03:32,890
that's just a fancy word for "knee-shaped
bumps on the side".

51
00:03:32,890 --> 00:03:36,750
The right bump receives data from the right
halves of the retinae of both eyes, the left

52
00:03:36,750 --> 00:03:38,410
bump from the left halves.

53
00:03:38,410 --> 00:03:42,160
The information is then forwarded to the visual
cortex in the back of the brain where it is

54
00:03:42,160 --> 00:03:44,970
processed and sent to the rest of the brain.

55
00:03:44,970 --> 00:03:49,251
Spatial and motion data are sent upwards,
where they serve to create a dynamic 3D model

56
00:03:49,251 --> 00:03:50,770
of the environment.

57
00:03:50,770 --> 00:03:56,900
Color and shape information is sent sidewards
and used to identify objects.

58
00:03:56,900 --> 00:03:57,900
scientific advice:

59
00:03:57,900 --> 00:03:59,861
An interesting field of research is optical
illusions.

60
00:03:59,861 --> 00:04:00,861
Take this one, for example.

61
00:04:00,861 --> 00:04:06,349
When you tell an earthling to fix the planet
in the center of the image, he will see a

62
00:04:06,349 --> 00:04:12,470
green orbiting saucer in the rotating free
slot between the pink ones - although there

63
00:04:12,470 --> 00:04:13,644
is no green saucer, only pink ones.

64
00:04:13,644 --> 00:04:17,500
The green is an after-image of the pink - maybe
due to the color contrast vision I will explain

65
00:04:17,500 --> 00:04:18,500
later.

66
00:04:18,500 --> 00:04:23,790
Sometimes the pink saucers will even disappear
and he will only see the green one.

67
00:04:23,790 --> 00:04:27,320
Earthlings always center both eyes onto one
spot in the visual field.

68
00:04:27,320 --> 00:04:31,050
The centers of the retinae have the highest
density of cones and provide the sharpest

69
00:04:31,050 --> 00:04:32,050
view.

70
00:04:32,050 --> 00:04:35,460
The farther you are away from the center,
the blurrier the vision gets.

71
00:04:35,460 --> 00:04:38,300
That's why earthlings always move their eyes
around.

72
00:04:38,300 --> 00:04:42,370
The brain does a good job in computing the
movement away, so the environment appears

73
00:04:42,370 --> 00:04:43,370
static.

74
00:04:43,370 --> 00:04:46,940
But this doesn't work when you poke the eyeball
slightly with a finger - in this case the

75
00:04:46,940 --> 00:04:49,830
world seems to move.

76
00:04:49,830 --> 00:04:54,520
As mentioned before, the data received by
the visual cortex are used for two purposes:

77
00:04:54,520 --> 00:04:58,290
Spatial orientation and motion data, and identifying
objects.

78
00:04:58,290 --> 00:05:00,450
Let's start with the former one.

79
00:05:00,450 --> 00:05:04,180
For spatial orientation, having two eyes comes
in handy:

80
00:05:04,180 --> 00:05:08,130
The brain uses the slight differences between
the data from both eyes to estimate the distance

81
00:05:08,130 --> 00:05:09,930
of different objects.

82
00:05:09,930 --> 00:05:14,180
Other input data are also taken into account,
in particular the smaller angular size of

83
00:05:14,180 --> 00:05:15,750
distant objects.

84
00:05:15,750 --> 00:05:20,560
The brain uses those data to construct a dynamic
3D model of the environment.

85
00:05:20,560 --> 00:05:22,880
Most animals have similar visual systems.

86
00:05:22,880 --> 00:05:28,020
Predators often have frontal eyes with overlapping
fields of view, to provide an optimal 3D vision

87
00:05:28,020 --> 00:05:29,020
in order to seize their prey.

88
00:05:29,020 --> 00:05:34,449
Prey animals, on the other hand, have often
lateral eyes to increase the field of view,

89
00:05:34,449 --> 00:05:37,120
so they can detect whoever wants to eat them.

90
00:05:37,120 --> 00:05:42,320
Except for the microbes.

91
00:05:42,320 --> 00:05:45,550
Now to the second point: identifying objects.

92
00:05:45,550 --> 00:05:49,800
This happens in the temporal cortex - that's
just a fancy word for "on the sides of the

93
00:05:49,800 --> 00:05:50,900
head".

94
00:05:50,900 --> 00:05:53,930
Earthling brains are powerful pattern-recognition
machines.

95
00:05:53,930 --> 00:05:57,520
We have already seen that the eyes send contour
data to the brain.

96
00:05:57,520 --> 00:06:02,979
What happens is that identified simple contour
patterns - corners, edges etc. - are assembled

97
00:06:02,979 --> 00:06:06,030
into more and more complex patterns.

98
00:06:06,030 --> 00:06:10,360
Earthlings are great at identifying shapes
even from incomplete contour elements.

99
00:06:10,360 --> 00:06:15,100
That's important, for example for identifying
partially hidden animals.

100
00:06:15,100 --> 00:06:18,639
When the initial contour elements are not
properly alligned, the brain has problems

101
00:06:18,639 --> 00:06:20,730
assembling the overall shape.

102
00:06:20,730 --> 00:06:26,250
Those lines, for example, appear as spirals,
but they are actually circles.

103
00:06:26,250 --> 00:06:31,620
The pattern recognition of faces is well developped,
as it contributes to the recognition of individuals.

104
00:06:31,620 --> 00:06:35,370
Earthling scientists have identified a neuron
in a brain that reacts to the celebrity Halle

105
00:06:35,370 --> 00:06:38,370
Berry, but not to images of other Earthlings.

106
00:06:38,370 --> 00:06:43,250
The neuron also reacts to Halle Berry in a
feline costume covering most of her face,

107
00:06:43,250 --> 00:06:44,670
as well as to her name.

108
00:06:44,670 --> 00:06:48,470
So, this cell seems to be a really big fan
of Halle Berry.

109
00:06:48,470 --> 00:06:52,870
They also found a neuron that likes Jennifer
Aniston, and another one that admires Ronald

110
00:06:52,870 --> 00:06:54,630
Reagan.

111
00:06:54,630 --> 00:06:57,270
Recognition of things is mainly based onto
shape and color.

112
00:06:57,270 --> 00:07:00,370
The concept of color can be confusing for
aliens.

113
00:07:00,370 --> 00:07:04,660
Most educated earthlings would agree that
color is a physical property of light.

114
00:07:04,660 --> 00:07:07,610
But as we will see, that is utter nonsense.

115
00:07:07,610 --> 00:07:11,180
Color isn't about physics - it's about biology!

116
00:07:11,180 --> 00:07:15,040
Earthling color perception can be compared
to how the Gloobobs of Aldaris 7 perceive

117
00:07:15,040 --> 00:07:16,080
sound.

118
00:07:16,080 --> 00:07:19,070
Gloobobs are known for having the worst brass
bands in the Galaxy.

119
00:07:19,070 --> 00:07:22,800
It's not their fault: Those creatures have
a very primitive audio perception and can

120
00:07:22,800 --> 00:07:30,940
only distinguish three ranges of frequencies,
called Ged, Bleen, and Droo.

121
00:07:30,940 --> 00:07:35,120
Every sound, every chord or melody they hear
will be reduced in their ears to a mix off

122
00:07:35,120 --> 00:07:37,389
Ged, Bleen and Droo.

123
00:07:37,389 --> 00:07:42,810
The Gloobob ears contain sound receptors for
each one of the three pitch ranges.

124
00:07:42,810 --> 00:07:47,850
The sensibilities of the receptors are somewhat
fuzzy, so they can tell single sounds apart.

125
00:07:47,850 --> 00:07:49,960
For example, when you play a scale...

126
00:07:49,960 --> 00:07:58,639
...Gloobobs hear this:

127
00:07:58,639 --> 00:08:01,210
But they are completely lost when it comes
to chords.

128
00:08:01,210 --> 00:08:04,710
Two notes are already too much.

129
00:08:04,710 --> 00:08:09,509
Take for example a chord consisting of Ged
and Bleen - for Gloobob ears, that sounds

130
00:08:09,509 --> 00:08:13,610
exactly like "Nello", halfway between Ged
and Bleen.

131
00:08:13,610 --> 00:08:19,560
So, for Gloobobs, Ged plus Bleen equals Nello,
which is of course nonsense - the only thing

132
00:08:19,560 --> 00:08:23,569
that is equal is the perception of the sounds
by Gloobob ears.

133
00:08:23,569 --> 00:08:27,710
Gloobob scientists have theorized that all
sounds belong to a three dimensional "sound

134
00:08:27,710 --> 00:08:31,430
space", defined by the perceived intensity
of Ged, Bleen and Droo.

135
00:08:31,430 --> 00:08:34,830
Mind, this isn't physics - it's biology.

136
00:08:34,830 --> 00:08:39,330
Gloobob sound recording devices can only produce
three sounds - enough to imitate sounds for

137
00:08:39,330 --> 00:08:42,289
Gloobob ears, but not for everybody else.

138
00:08:42,289 --> 00:08:46,560
The same holds for Gloobob instruments - hence
the bad brass bands.

139
00:08:46,560 --> 00:08:48,260
Why am I telling you this?

140
00:08:48,260 --> 00:08:50,760
Because earthling vision works the same.

141
00:08:50,760 --> 00:08:54,629
Earthlings have only three kinds of color
receptors, often called - not quite correctly

142
00:08:54,629 --> 00:08:57,010
- red, green and blue.

143
00:08:57,010 --> 00:09:01,080
Even the most complex combination of frequencies
are reduced by earthling eyes to a combination

144
00:09:01,080 --> 00:09:03,130
of red, green and blue.

145
00:09:03,130 --> 00:09:06,970
For example, earthlings cannot distinguish
between monochromatic yellow light and a mix

146
00:09:06,970 --> 00:09:08,550
of red and green light.

147
00:09:08,550 --> 00:09:12,770
In both cases, the red and green receptors
are excited in the same way.

148
00:09:12,770 --> 00:09:16,209
That's why earthlings say that "red plus green
equals yellow".

149
00:09:16,209 --> 00:09:18,529
This is biology, not physics.

150
00:09:18,529 --> 00:09:23,020
In other words, color isn't a physical property
- it only exists in the brain.

151
00:09:23,020 --> 00:09:27,430
Actually, the expression "red receptor" is
misleading - this receptor's peak is rather

152
00:09:27,430 --> 00:09:29,330
in the green-yellow range.

153
00:09:29,330 --> 00:09:32,209
This reduces an effect called chromatic aberration.

154
00:09:32,209 --> 00:09:36,500
But anyway, what is sent to the brain is not
the raw receptor response but color contrast

155
00:09:36,500 --> 00:09:43,040
data - more precisely, yellow-blue contrast,
red-green contrast, and luminosity contrast.

156
00:09:43,040 --> 00:09:46,420
But what is the advantage of sending color
contrast data?

157
00:09:46,420 --> 00:09:50,440
To understand this, we have to understand
what color actually is.

158
00:09:50,440 --> 00:09:54,670
When you ask educated adult earthlings what
color is, they will probably brabble something

159
00:09:54,670 --> 00:09:58,440
about frequencies, color circles and additive
color blending.

160
00:09:58,440 --> 00:10:02,680
But when you ask earthling cubs, they will
talk about blue teddies, yellow flowers and

161
00:10:02,680 --> 00:10:04,140
pink sofas.

162
00:10:04,140 --> 00:10:09,200
In other words, they see color not as a property
of light, but as a property of objects.

163
00:10:09,200 --> 00:10:11,660
And that's actually a much better approach.

164
00:10:11,660 --> 00:10:16,930
See, when an earthling has a pink car, it
will always be a pink car, no matter how it

165
00:10:16,930 --> 00:10:20,180
is lit.

166
00:10:20,180 --> 00:10:22,000
Earthling visions relies on whatever light
source is available.

167
00:10:22,000 --> 00:10:31,200
The reflected light might differ, but for
the earthling, his car will always have the

168
00:10:31,200 --> 00:10:32,200
same color.

169
00:10:32,200 --> 00:10:35,180
So, the word "pink" doesn't actually describe
light - it describes how the surface reacts

170
00:10:35,180 --> 00:10:38,269
to varying light, as perceived by the earthling
eye.

171
00:10:38,269 --> 00:10:42,670
So, color is a property of surfaces, which
exists only in the brain.

172
00:10:42,670 --> 00:10:43,810
How is this even possible ?

173
00:10:43,810 --> 00:10:48,330
Well, what happens is that the brain takes
the sensor information and computes the lighting

174
00:10:48,330 --> 00:10:49,330
away.

175
00:10:49,330 --> 00:10:53,950
What remains is a perceived property of surfaces,
an imaginary material invariant - color.

176
00:10:53,950 --> 00:10:59,370
Here, the color contrast data comes in handy:
No matter the lighting, a pink sofa is always

177
00:10:59,370 --> 00:11:03,209
pinker than the green carpet it is standing
on.

178
00:11:03,209 --> 00:11:07,670
Color is a good example of how earthlings
construct a model of reality in their brain.

179
00:11:07,670 --> 00:11:11,510
Physical objects are collections of atoms
with properties like shape, size and spectral

180
00:11:11,510 --> 00:11:13,620
characteristics of the surface.

181
00:11:13,620 --> 00:11:18,490
But the brain can't directly access to those
properties - all it has is sensor information.

182
00:11:18,490 --> 00:11:23,240
So it takes this information, computes factors
like lighting and distance away, and constructs

183
00:11:23,240 --> 00:11:25,910
simplified models of the objects in the world.

184
00:11:25,910 --> 00:11:30,680
The imaginary properties of the object models
correspond more or less to physical reality.

185
00:11:30,680 --> 00:11:35,000
Size and shape are rather accurate approximation
of an object's actual geometry, but color

186
00:11:35,000 --> 00:11:38,160
is a rough simplification of it's spectral
characteristics.

187
00:11:38,160 --> 00:11:42,200
So, color is an imaginary property of materials.

188
00:11:42,200 --> 00:11:47,260
This makes sense, as the main purpose of color
is actually the identification of materials.

189
00:11:47,260 --> 00:11:51,620
Color allows finding things like flintstone,
fertile earth or ripe fruits.

190
00:11:51,620 --> 00:11:55,339
The brain takes out the lighting information
to obtain the lighting-invariant "color" and

191
00:11:55,339 --> 00:12:00,640
tell different materials apart - even if the
reflected light is actually the same.

192
00:12:00,640 --> 00:12:02,610
Colors have a high symbolic meaning.

193
00:12:02,610 --> 00:12:06,550
Blue is perceived as calm and cool, as lakes
and oceans are blue.

194
00:12:06,550 --> 00:12:10,170
Green is associated with nature, because plants
are green.

195
00:12:10,170 --> 00:12:14,610
Yellow is perceived as joyful and energetic,
because earth orbits a yellow star.

196
00:12:14,610 --> 00:12:22,779
Red is associated with violence and danger,
as red is the color of fire and blood.

197
00:12:22,779 --> 00:12:26,650
Fictional characters are sometimes color-coded
for easy identification.

198
00:12:26,650 --> 00:12:30,660
Cartoon characters can often be identified
with little more than color information - even

199
00:12:30,660 --> 00:12:32,370
humanized animals.

200
00:12:32,370 --> 00:12:37,310
This works also for some live action characters,
especially when they wear some sort of uniform.

201
00:12:37,310 --> 00:12:40,990
Colors play also an important part in earthlings'
social life.

202
00:12:40,990 --> 00:12:44,020
For example, lovers like to give each other
colorful flowers.

203
00:12:44,020 --> 00:12:47,570
There isn't any practical sense, as you can't
eat flowers.

204
00:12:47,570 --> 00:12:50,279
There is an old saying amongst alien anthropologists:

205
00:12:50,279 --> 00:12:53,779
If it doesn't make sense, it's probably a
ritual.

206
00:12:53,779 --> 00:12:56,170
Tips for tourists.

207
00:12:56,170 --> 00:13:00,760
If you want to watch an earthling movie, don't
expect realistic colors:

208
00:13:00,760 --> 00:13:03,680
Earthling cameras can only record three color
components.

209
00:13:03,680 --> 00:13:07,779
Personally, I find black-and-white movies
less disturbing.

210
00:13:07,779 --> 00:13:12,860
Above all, stay away from so-called 3D movies,
especially if you have only one eye.

211
00:13:12,860 --> 00:13:18,120
It shall be noted that some female earthlings
have four types of cones instead of three.

212
00:13:18,120 --> 00:13:21,860
In earthling terms, they have a four-dimensional
color space.

213
00:13:21,860 --> 00:13:25,860
There are also accounds on individuals able
to perceive an additional color called octarine.

214
00:13:25,860 --> 00:13:31,160
But the same accounts also report an unregistered
habitable planar super-structure with bio-propulsion,

215
00:13:31,160 --> 00:13:34,380
as well as other oddities, so this is probably
fiction.

216
00:13:34,380 --> 00:13:38,310
Anyway, this is nothing compared with an aquatic
animal called the mantis shrimp which has

217
00:13:38,310 --> 00:13:42,420
a sixteen-dimensional color space.

218
00:13:42,420 --> 00:13:44,040
Strategic advice.

219
00:13:44,040 --> 00:13:46,829
Mantis shrimps would make a good base to breed
super-soldiers:

220
00:13:46,829 --> 00:13:50,020
Their color vision would make earthling camouflage
useless,

221
00:13:50,020 --> 00:13:54,660
they have sharp appendages they can accelerate
to the speed of earthlings weapons projectiles,

222
00:13:54,660 --> 00:13:56,339
they wear a natural body armour,

223
00:13:56,339 --> 00:13:59,510
and they can move so fast that the liquid
around them starts boiling.

224
00:13:59,510 --> 00:14:02,380
However, you might want to do something about
their size.

225
00:14:02,380 --> 00:14:04,940
I will conclude with an open question:

226
00:14:04,940 --> 00:14:08,769
Spectral violet, the light at the upper end
of the visual spectrum, is allegedly perceived

227
00:14:08,769 --> 00:14:10,339
as slightly reddish.

228
00:14:10,339 --> 00:14:13,899
That's why earthlings bend the spectrum to
a circle - the color wheel.

229
00:14:13,899 --> 00:14:18,339
But violet light is far off the so-called
red receptors - why is it perceived as reddish?

230
00:14:18,339 --> 00:14:20,089
I see two possibilities.

231
00:14:20,089 --> 00:14:23,850
Either the red receptors have a second bump
in the violet zone.

232
00:14:23,850 --> 00:14:27,900
Or spectral violet isn't actually perceived
as reddish blue, but as deep blue, and the

233
00:14:27,900 --> 00:14:30,290
name "violet" is actually a misnomer.

234
00:14:30,290 --> 00:14:34,960
The fact that computer screens can't display
spectral violet might add to the confusion.

235
00:14:34,960 --> 00:14:36,640
I honestly don't know.

236
00:14:36,640 --> 00:14:39,950
So I'll ask my earthling viewers: What do
you think?

237
00:14:39,950 --> 00:14:45,150
And if you have, say, access to a violet laser,
or a violet light weapon : Does spectral violet

238
00:14:45,150 --> 00:14:48,209
actually appear reddish, or rather deep blue?

239
00:14:48,209 --> 00:14:50,480
If it's reddish: How comes?

240
00:14:50,480 --> 00:14:53,280
If it's deep blue: Why the color wheel?

241
00:14:53,280 --> 00:14:55,779
This was the twelveth episode of Earthlings
101.

242
00:14:55,779 --> 00:15:01,650
Next time we will speak about earthling mathematics
- a science of truth, space, numbers, and

243
00:15:01,650 --> 00:15:02,940
the gender of Blobblings.

244
00:15:02,940 --> 00:15:07,720
Thanks for watching, click on "like" if you
liked it, and as always: Don't forget to be

245
00:15:07,720 --> 00:15:26,639
alien!

